      "id": "n5",
      "type": "text",
      "content": {
        "markdown": "The reservation orchestrator coordinates a reservation from start to finish. It asks the stock ledger to reserve the requested quantity, asks the pricing rules for the order's price, and, once both succeed, publishes a StockReserved event to the message broker. If the ledger cannot reserve the full quantity, the orchestrator rejects the whole order; it never makes a partial reservation. A reservation that is not confirmed within 15 minutes is released by the ledger and the stock becomes available again."
      }
    },
